      <div class="col-lg-6 content">
        <h2>A Farm Built Around a Way of Life</h2>
        <p>
          Smoky Mountain Acres began with a simple desire: to raise animals, grow food, and understand more honestly what happens between the pasture and the kitchen. Our family is building a farmstead in the foothills of East Tennessee where animal care, land stewardship, and everyday family life belong in the same picture.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not trying to make farming look effortless or turn a few attractive words into a guarantee. We are trying to make our choices understandable: give animals meaningful access to pasture, feed them responsibly, use fewer outside inputs where we can, and stay honest about what our practices and labels do and do not mean.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i> <span>Pigs, chickens, and sheep are raised with pasture access and room for natural behavior.</span></li>
          <li><i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i> <span>Supplemental feed is organic and appropriate for each species, without implying USDA Organic certification.</span></li>
          <li><i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i> <span>We do not use synthetic fertilizers or pesticides on our farm and manage the land through observation, animal movement, and rest.</span></li>
          <li><i class="bi bi-check2-all"></i> <span>We want visitors, customers, and our own family to know how the animals live and what goes into their care.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

