          alt="Mountain view near Cosby, Tennessee">
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-1 content">
        <h2>Still Growing, Still Learning</h2>
        <p>
          A real farm changes with the weather, the soil, the animals, and the people caring for them. Pasture is stronger in some seasons than others. A flock lays differently through the year. A growing animal may need more than the land can provide at a particular moment.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are building our systems around that seasonal reality instead of pretending it is not there. That means moving animals, resting ground, providing hay or supplemental feed when needed, and making decisions based on the health of the animals and land in front of us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our hope is that Smoky Mountain Acres becomes a productive, welcoming farm where people can understand not only what we offer, but why we raise animals this way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
